 "limits": [
  "judges the object it read, not the final LTO'd and linked speaker ELF: the root release profile sets lto = true and strip = \"symbols\", and under lto = true rustc writes LLVM bitcode (refused here), so an object that can be read was built with LTO off; the shipped ELF is fat-LTO'd and may inline differently",
  "attribution is per surviving function: a function inlined into its caller is judged as part of the caller; an extra widen, multiply, add, subtract or narrow contributed by inlined non-Section code is not visible to the helper-set rule",
  "reachability follows relocations in executable sections, a call and an address taken alike (so it over-approximates); an indirect call through a pointer is not resolved. Helper counts are CALL SITES in the object (one per R_MIPS_26 or CALL16), not executions",
  "no numerical or instruction-count claim is made"
 ],
 "notes": [
  "Built from a git archive export of 53f83cf plus the d02-softfloat-check v4 patch (sha256 812eafc9fb051c69...), central run b56, one worker. The build script is unchanged since; this record was read by the v5 checker, because the v4 checker crashed rendering the rlib's text report.",
